I. SOURCE HIERARCHY

LAYER 0 — OFFICIAL / MECHANICAL EARNINGS BASE
Sourced by Claude from:
- Company 8-K / earnings release (SEC EDGAR)
- Official earnings deck
- Reliable wire summary (Reuters, CNBC, Yahoo Finance)
- Motley Fool transcript if available

Must include where confirmable:
- Revenue (reported and organic/constant currency if disclosed)
- EPS (GAAP and adjusted)
- Key operating metrics (segment revenue, margin, KPIs)
- Guidance (Q+1 and full year) ◆◆◆ with raise-composition decomposition where derivable (§12)
- Consensus beat/miss (label source explicitly)
◆◆◆ - Contracted-demand instruments where disclosed: RPO/cRPO/backlog dollars with QoQ and YoY bases BOTH stated (never one growth basis unlabelled), composition notes (e.g., "sequential growth driven by non-AI-lab clients"), and per-quarter additions where derivable

If consensus not confirmed: "Consensus not confirmed at tape construction"
If key figure not confirmed: "Actual not confirmed at tape construction"
Reliability: High (official source) or Medium (wire summary only)

◆ Stock reaction in Layer 0: Stock reaction must include initial AH (if applicable), extended AH (if applicable), and next-session close (if available). If only one window is available at tape construction, state the window explicitly. Do not present a single number as the verdict when multiple windows exist. ◆◆◆ Setup context (YTD move, distance from high/low, run-in to the print, options-implied move, short-interest direction where retrieved) is part of the Layer 0 reaction block, not an optional flourish — the pricing regime (§XVI) cannot be applied without it.

◆◆◆ EU / non-US names — mandatory additions to Layer 0:
- FX TRIPLE RECONCILIATION: reported growth = organic + FX + perimeter, decomposed explicitly (e.g., "reported −3% = organic +2%, FX −5%, perimeter −1%"). The organic line is the demand statement; the reported line is a translation artifact. Company-quantified FX EBIT guidance captured where given.
- Semi-annual reporters (H1 + implied Q2 organic): state both the H1 figures and the derived/disclosed Q2 organic; label derivations.
- Dual-listing reaction split per §11 (local line vs ADR), each labelled.
- EU sell-side named-voice access is structurally thinner in readable sources: the voice-floor flag is expected more often; state it honestly and offer rescout.

