LAYER 1 — OFFICIAL ENRICHMENT
Add official detail not fully visible in the base block:
- Segment composition and margin detail
- Guide wording and assumptions
- Capex / buyback / dividend detail
- Management priorities and prepared remarks
- KPIs and business-line detail explicitly disclosed
- Named source of any material non-operating item in EPS. If not disclosed officially, run one additional targeted search and label result. If still unconfirmed: "Non-operating item source not confirmed at tape construction"
◆◆◆ - §13 family classification and usage doctrine per §13-ter
◆◆◆ - Transmission-chain contribution: where the print evidences a link in a documented chain (§XVI-B), state the link explicitly ("the memory-cost admission is the MU thesis appearing as a hyperscaler budget line")

Sources: earnings release, deck, transcript prepared remarks, 8-K exhibits only.
Reliability: High

◆ Strategic shift detection: Layer 1 must explicitly flag any reversal of a prior management doctrine or multi-year stated strategy, even when not headline-worthy in the press release. Examples observed in 2026 cohort:
- MSTR: "never sell BTC" doctrine reversed
- PFE: Vyndamax LOE extended 2.5 years restructures 2026–2029 bridge
- META: 10% workforce cut alongside CapEx raise signals AI-first labor reallocation; ◆◆◆ later: 2027 capex frame withheld (opacity as doctrine)
- DIS: First D'Amaro earnings call as CEO — strategic framework debut
- AAPL/MSTR/PYPL pattern: New CEO admitting "years of underinvestment" is a multi-year restructuring signal
◆◆◆ - GOOGL: buyback suspension (capital-return doctrine break)
◆◆◆ - ASML/NFLX: disclosure-metric retirement (bookings / engagement) — information-regime downgrade
◆◆◆ - MCD: same-day executive change delivered WITH a miss (accountability instrument) + "not a strategy problem" doctrine defense
◆◆◆ - Bastian: low-cost-model obituary; Wei: multi-year demand-wall declaration; structural-regime statements replacing quarter commentary are a late-cycle marker — flag them as a class
- These shifts often matter more than the quarterly print for the medium-term thesis.

◆◆ Relay labeling rule: When an official release or transcript is accessed via a republication (Yahoo, Benzinga, StockTitan, Investing.com), label it: "Full-text relay — original source: [name]." A relay clearly reproducing the current official release may support Layer 1 at Medium-High reliability. Never label a relay as the official source. Yahoo/relay and original count as one underlying source, not two.

