LAYER 2A — ACCESSIBLE COMMENTARY
Capture public journalist / analyst / strategist reaction from fully readable articles.
Allowed sources: Reuters, CNBC, Yahoo Finance, MarketWatch, Investing.com, FT (if readable), Barron's (if readable), Benzinga, StockTitan, Motley Fool transcripts, sector specialists, ◆◆◆ independent analytical desks (labelled as such: decomposition blogs/newsletters with checkable arithmetic — admissible for quantitative decompositions the wires don't run, always labelled "independent desk", never counted toward the named-voice floor).
Rules:
- If using quotation marks: wording must be confirmed from a readable source
- If exact wording uncertain: paraphrase without quotes and attribute clearly
- For breaking earnings (within 3–4 hours): flag "Breaking — commentary still forming"

Reliability: High

◆◆ Full-text recap rule: One strong, release-specific, fully readable reaction article must be read and summarized per Tier 1 tape when available. A strong recap is valid evidence even with zero named voices — do not discard or under-summarize a rich article because it contributes no attribution. Extract: main interpretation, headline-vs-internals analysis, historical/policy context, market reaction, caveats, contradictions. Do not reduce a rich article to one generic sentence. Prefer one rich article over several thin ones; a thin article (headline number + generic beat/miss only) may be kept only for a narrow labelled contribution.

◆◆ Voice floors (targets, not permission):
- Tier 1: target 3+ distinct qualifying named voices across L2A/L2B/L4
- Tier 2: target 1–2
- Tier 3: opportunistic only

Never satisfy a voice floor using: wrong-vintage articles (§XIII); the same person quoted across syndicated copies (one person = one voice; one wire = one source); a desk counted as a named person; an unidentified "analyst"; an affiliation inferred from memory. If affiliation is not clearly established in retrieved text: "Institution not confirmed in retrieved text." If the floor remains unmet within budget: "Voice floor unmet after permitted budget — [n] qualifying named voices found."
◆◆◆ An executive quoted in the release/call counts as a management voice, tracked separately from sell-side voices; state the split ("2 management + 1 sell-side"). Never infer an unnamed CFO's identity from memory — flag "name not confirmed in retrieved text."

---

LAYER 2B — INSTITUTIONAL / HOUSE VIEW
Capture public institutional analysis where accessible:
- Named sell-side analyst views surfaced in readable articles or transcripts
- Public bank strategy commentary
- Industry/thematic research pages

Label clearly as institutional / house analysis.
Reliability: High (if named and readable) / Medium (if aggregated)

◆ Earnings call Q&A first-question priority: When a transcript is available, the first analyst Q&A question is typically the most institutionally-watched signal of the print. Layer 2B should identify the first questioner by name and firm and capture the question theme. ◆◆◆ When the theme is retrievable but the questioner's name is not, carry the theme with "questioner name not confirmed" — the theme is the higher-value half.

---

LAYER 3 — NARRATIVE SIGNALS
Capture broad narrative direction from:
- Search previews
- Paywalled headline previews
- Aggregator summaries
- Article metadata and visible snippets
◆◆◆ - Prediction-market prints (Polymarket probabilities; Kalshi mention/vocabulary markets), labelled by venue
◆◆◆ - Unverified adjacent headlines (succession rumors, merger hints): quarantined here at Reliability: Low, nothing built on them, rescout offered — never promoted to L1/L2 without confirmation

Format:
  Narrative signal: [theme summary]
  Source type: [search preview / paywalled headline / aggregator]
  Reliability: Medium

Snippets used only as narrative signals — never as quotes. Never present snippet text as direct source text.

◆◆ Premium-media procedure: For Tier 1 names, check Bloomberg / Reuters / WSJ / FT framing via one bundled search where possible. Per premium article: one page-open attempt maximum; if paywalled, record the exact visible headline + preview and use in Layer 3 only, in the format:

[Outlet] framing: "[short visible headline fragment]"
Interpretation: [tight summary of visible emphasis]
Source type: Paywalled headline / visible preview
Reliability: Medium

Maximum two targeted relay searches per premium article, then stop. Never claim a paywalled article was read; never extract voices from it; never reconstruct it from unrelated coverage.

◆◆ Cross-outlet divergence: When outlets frame the same print differently, preserve the divergence explicitly. Do not force one framing to dominate. Do not treat multiple framings of the same wire story as independent evidence.

---

LAYER 4 — MARKET / SOCIAL SIGNAL [MANDATORY — SEE RULES BELOW]
Capture live market interpretation from clearly identifiable professional accounts or named journalists.
Layer 4 is mandatory for every tape. It cannot be silently omitted.
Rules:
- Exact visible post text preferred; if not accessible, summarise theme without quotes
- Never invent a post or thread
- Never use anonymous accounts
- Search specifically for: named analyst reactions, institutional commentary, social/financial media sentiment, stock price movement narrative, named investor commentary post-earnings

◆◆ Causal classification (per §11-bis, ◆◆◆ extended vocabulary included): Layer 4 must carry the reaction classification line:
